{{- /*
  Poolers. This build ships no Pooler observer, so it makes no claim
  about connection poolers — the screen says exactly that rather than
  rendering an empty result that could be read as "no poolers exist".
  One honest not-observed state serves the overview, pods, and logs
  entries; the sidebar's current marker is the only thing that differs.
*/ -}}
{{template "page-head" "poolers"}}
{{template "shell-open" .Shell}}
    <section class="panel">
      <h2>Poolers</h2>
      <div class="empty"><strong>Poolers are not observed in this build</strong>This console has no PgBouncer <code>Pooler</code> observer, so it makes no claim about connection poolers for this cluster — neither that any exist nor that none do. Applications reach the database services directly unless a pooler is deployed and a future build observes it.</div>
    </section>
{{template "shell-close"}}
